// S3 control -- "Scattered larder", `Reports/lab-behaviour-scenarios-2026-09-06.md`.
// `far_larder.ron`'s paired control: the identical colony and the identical
// mass of food, spread evenly along the ground instead of piled at the far
// wall. A route can form over a heap and cannot form over an even spread,
// so the difference between the two overlays is the trail-following
// question's own measurement, not a guess about it.
//
// **The colony sits at x: 107, the same fix and the same reason as
// `far_larder.ron`**: x: 40 placed only 35 of 52 ants (the 52-ant band is
// 204 cells wide and ran off the world's west edge), and x: 107 is the
// smallest column at which the identical bed and colony place all 52 --
// confirmed with a rebuilt `labshot` against this file too, not assumed
// from the paired file.
//
// **Food per 6,000-frame window**: identical mass to `far_larder.ron`'s
// heap, so the same arithmetic applies -- 60 cells at build (57,600) then
// 30 every 6,000 frames (28,800, 92.3% of the colony's 52 * 0.10 * 6000 =
// 31,200 idle burn), already over half.
(
    name: "scattered_larder",
    title: "SCATTERED LARDER",
    question: "The far larder's own food, spread evenly instead of piled -- does the route on the pheromone overlay disappear?",
    bed: (
        width: 512,
        height: 320,
        soil_depth: 96,
        ground_y: 160,
        compartments: 1,
        founders: 0,
        species: "herb",
        colonies: 0,
        colony_ants: 52,
        colony_species: "ant",
        predators: 0,
        lamp_spacing: 33,
        seed: 1,
        extra_walls: [],
    ),
    settings: [],
    placements: [
        Colony(species: "ant", x: 107, count: 52),
        Scatter(material: "windfall", x0: 60, x1: 480, cells: 60),
    ],
    timeline: [
        (at: 6000, every: 6000, until: 0, what: Scatter(material: "windfall", x0: 60, x1: 480, cells: 30)),
    ],
